# retroforge: enable seatd on release as the session's seat broker (SteamOS layer B). The gamescope
# launcher (run as the player user by retroforge-session.service) opens the DRM seat via this
# persistent root seatd.service (ExecStart=seatd -g seat); player is in the `seat` group.
# /etc/machine-id is empty on a fresh image so systemd runs preset-all on
# first boot, where the stock 99-default.preset is "disable *"; this higher-priority preset (60 < 99)
# keeps seatd enabled. A build-time multi-user.target.wants symlink ships alongside as a fallback
# (cf. inputplumber's 60-retroforge).
enable seatd.service
